---
title: Air Fryer Baked Potato
source: https://preppykitchen.com/air-fryer-baked-potato/#recipe
servings: 4
time required: 55 minutes
course: Side Dish
cuisine: American
---

Scrub the @potato{4}(medium russet) well. Then, either air dry or dry with a towel before proceeding. 

Preheat your #air fryer{} to 400°F. 

Prick the potatoes all over, 5 to 6 times each, with a fork. Brush the @olive oil{1%tbsp} evenly all over the potatoes, and sprinkle with @sea salt{1%tsp}. 

Place the potatoes in the basket of the air fryer, leaving about a ½-inch of space in between each potato. Cook at 400°F for ~{25%minutes}. 

Flip the potatoes and continue to cook for another ~{20-25%minutes} or until they are tender and a paring knife is easily inserted into the potatoes. 

Let the potatoes cool for ~{5%minutes}. Cut a lengthwise slit across the top of the potato. Squeeze the sides towards the center to open the potatoes, and fluff the interior with a fork. 

Top with @?butter{}, @?sour cream{}, @?chives{}, @?cheese{}, and/or @?crumbled bacon{} as desired. 

> Optional toppings include Italian seasoning, oregano, freshly ground pepper, or chili powder.